    "answer": {
      "short": "$1+x+x^2=\\dfrac{x^3-1}{x-1}$, $x\\ne1$.\n\nExpand the product to obtain $x^3-1$, then divide by the nonzero factor $x-1$.",
      "worked": "Expanding the product gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(1+x+x^2)&=x+x^2+x^3-1-x-x^2\\\\(x-1)(1+x+x^2)&=x^3-1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x\\ne1$, divide by $x-1$:\n$$1+x+x^2=\\frac{x^3-1}{x-1}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
